\title{What false dependencies does register renaming eliminate?}
\tag{card}
\meta{anki}{1784508017023}

\prompt{Write-after-write (#{\mathrm{WAW}}) and write-after-read (#{\mathrm{WAR}}) hazards — the \em{false} dependencies that arise from reusing an architectural register, not from real data flow. Removing them exposes more [[5CT9]] to the scheduler.}
